==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|richten}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|rihten}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*rihtijaną||to right}}, derived from {{m|gem-pro|*rehtaz||right, straight}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|nl|recht|t1=straight|-en|t2=deadjectival|id2=deadjectival}} and shows the effect of historical [[i-mutation]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈrɪxtə(n)/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-richten.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɪxtən|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{nl-verb}}

# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[direct]], [[aim]]
#: {{syn|nl|doelen|munten}}

====Conjugation====
{{nl-conj-wk|richt}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|nl|richting}}
* {{l|nl|aanrichten}}
* {{l|nl|africhten}}
* {{l|nl|berichten}}
* {{l|nl|gelijkrichten}}
* {{l|nl|inrichten}}
* {{l|nl|oprichten}}
* {{l|nl|uitrichten}}
* {{l|nl|verrichten}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|af|rig}}
* {{desc|dcr|richt}}

{{cln|nl|i-mutated deadjectival verbs}}

==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|inh=1}}
{{inh|de|gmh|richten}}, from {{inh|de|goh|rihten}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*rihtijan||to right}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|right}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[ˈʁɪçtn̩]|[ˈʁɪçtən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-richten.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|de|rich|ten}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[direct]], to [[point]] {{+obj|de|acc<e.g. a weapon> + :auf(acc)<at someone/something>}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Richte''' diese Waffe nicht auf mich!|Don't '''point''' that gun at me!}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[fix]], to [[rectify]], to [[put right]]
#: {{ux|de|Wer kann diese Krise '''richten'''?|Who can '''solve''' this crisis?}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[straighten]] (something bent or tilted or not lined up properly); to [[right]]
#: {{ux|de|Kannst du den Löffel auch '''richten'''?|Can you also '''straighten''' the spoon?}}
#: {{ux|de|[[zugrunde]] '''richten'''.|to '''destroy''' (to level to the ground).}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to be [[directed]] (at) {{q|of emotions, words, etc.}}; to [[turn]] (toward) {{q|of a look, one's eyes, gaze, etc.}} {{+obj|de|:auf(acc)/:gegen(acc)<someone>}}
#: {{ux|de|Keine Sorge, ihre Wut '''richtet sich''' nicht gegen Sie.|Don't worry, her anger '''is'''n't '''directed''' at you.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[judge]]
#: {{syn|de|urteilen}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[follow]] the [[lead]] of, to [[abide]] by {{gl|to adjust one's behavior according to a person, rule etc.}} {{+obj|de|:nach}}
#: {{uxi|de|Das ist mir egal; ich '''richte mich''' nach dir.|I don’t care; I will '''follow''' your '''lead'''.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[depend]] {{+obj|de|:nach<on>}} {{q|impersonal}}
#: {{uxi|de|Der Wechselkurs '''richtet sich''' nach den politischen Geschehnissen.|The exchange rate '''depends''' on political events.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|dated|higher register}} to [[execute]], to [[put to death]]
#: {{syn|de|hinrichten}}

